WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.790
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.460
A trial to crown
the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.380
In the hopes of battling Dande,
the current Supreme Monarch,

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.720
Satoshi is participating
in the Championships.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.890
Trainers from all over the world
are taking part.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.060
They battle other trainers
in their class,

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.780
and the results of those battles...

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.730
...determine their
current ranking in the world.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:54.860
Satoshi and Kamonegi once met Rinto,
a trainer with an Earlade, and lost to him.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:01.240
To hone Kamonegi’s skills, Satoshi underwent training
with Gampi of the Kalos Elite Four.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:02.750
And...

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.620
Here. I’m glad it’s safe.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.710
That leek is what’s most
important to you, after all!

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:18.760
A knight is one who fights to protect their precious lord,
and the weak and powerless.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:25.520
When one truly treasures another, and fights to protect them,
their strength is magnified manyfold.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.850
The leek led Satoshi and Kamonegi
to form a strong bond.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.790
Satoshi is currently ranked 273th,
which places him in the Super Class.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.240
His path to the Monarch Dande
remains a long one.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:42.050
Satoshi and his Pokémon
continue their battles, even today!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.230
Looking good, Kamonegi!

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.430
Keep closing the distance!

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.940
Hassam, this is our chance!
Scissor Cross!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.360
Kamonegi! Use Detect!

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.070
Crossroad Kill!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.750
It hit!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.450
You did it!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.070
Hassam! You did great!

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.260
Oh... Sarunori,
do you want to battle too?

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.680
Satoshi, Kamonegi...
You two are really in sync.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.100
We are noble knights, after all!

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.290
Next stop: Leek Master!

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.070
Is that really how
being a Leek Master works?

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.040
Hey, if we say it works, it works!

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.370
Satoshi, let’s go to
the Pokémon Center.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.930
Hassam and Kamonegi
are both tired out from the battle.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.000
You’re right.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.240
Return, Kamonegi!

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.660
Return, Hassam.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.960
Pikachu?

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.650
There’s something in there,
isn’t there, Sarunori?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:14.420
Madatsubomi! Flower Pokémon!
Grass/Poison type!

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.620
It prefers hot and humid
environments!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.320
It moves very quickly
when capturing prey with its vines!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.650
But that Madatsubomi
looks kinda worn out...

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.510
That looks really soothing!

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.680
That reminds me, back then...

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.470
It got better!
That was great, Sarunori!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:13.310
That means Sarunori’s powers
even work on Pokémon!

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.170
Yeah.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.780
What is it, Sarunori?

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.690
You’ve already made friends?

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.050
Do you want me to...

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.350
This is great. Catch it!

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.250
Okay! Hold on, Sarunori...

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.550
Monster Ball, go!

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.010
Great!

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.690
Madatsubomi’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.280
I caught Madatsubomi!

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:10.870
I hope we’ll be good friends,
Madatsubomi.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:17.680
Thank you for waiting!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.400
Hassam and Kamonegi
should be all better now!

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:21.800
Thank you, Miss Joy.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.290
Thank you.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.580
All right, come on out,
Kamonegi!

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.590
Glad you’re feeling better!

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.040
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:45.210
You’re...

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.850
Hang in there, Kamonegi!

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.370
Oh, yes.
I’ve battled you before.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.120
Yeah! It’s been a while, Rinto!

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.750
Huh.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.660
So you’re participating in
the Championships?

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.360
But I didn’t get
a notification last time...

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.420
I had only just entered at the time,

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.100
so I was still in the Normal Class.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.140
So now you’re in the Super Class?!

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.930
Yes. I see you are, too.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:24.770
Has Kamonegi been well?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.570
Better than well!

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:30.880
He’s even had training at Gampi’s place,
one of the Kalos Elite Four!

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.280
Oh, so you’ve been to
the Castle of Chivalry?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.340
You’ve heard of it?
We even got Knight Medals!

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:41.900
We also went through
some harsh training there.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.000
It brings back memories,
huh, Earlade?

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.300
Rinto! Let’s battle!

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.520
Me and Kamonegi
have both powered up!

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.130
It won’t go like it did last time!

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.770
I should hope so.

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:57.390
I look forward to
seeing your potential.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.840
Yeah! We’re gonna shock you!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:07.180
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Super Class battle!

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:12.180
The match-up is Contestant Rinto
VS Contestant Satoshi.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.530
Thanks, Go.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.540
Huh?

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:18.760
I wouldn’t be having this battle
if you hadn’t suggested going to the Pokémon Center.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.370
Right. Win it for me!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.680
Yeah!

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.790
Pikachu,
you’ll be watching us too, right?

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:31.890
This battle will be a 1v1.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:34.760
Both sides, send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:35.880
3!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.010
2!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.010
1!

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.590
Go!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:41.120
Go, Earlade!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.350
Aim to be Leek Master!

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.730
Battle, start!

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:52.230
I’ll have you demonstrate
how much you’ve improved.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.620
Bring it on!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:56.570
Consecutive Cut!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.780
Satoshi! Don’t let him control
the pace of the battle!

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:02.030
I know!

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:05.330
Earlade, brush it off!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.460
Crossroad Kill.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.300
Use Detect!

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.550
Psycho Cutter.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:38.070
Satoshi and Kamonegi have improved,
but Rinto and Earlade are still one step ahead!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.700
They changed tactics and
went straight for a counterattack...

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.450
Detect, huh?

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.360
But since you battle with brute-force,

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.830
if your leek gets deflected even once,
its weight throws you off balance.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.320
You truly are inadequate.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:57.590
If you’re gonna keep calling them inadequate,
why don’t you tell them <i>what</i> they’re lacking?!

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:01.840
I’m no Gym Leader.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.100
You can find the answer for yourself.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:06.850
Well then, this time it’s my turn.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.850
Earlade, Infight!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.690
Counter it! Crossroad Kill!

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:19.820
Detect!

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.320
Feint!

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:43.530
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:58.900
His leek...

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.990
He knew Feint...

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:06.370
That means he’ll just break through it
if Satoshi uses Detect...

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.370
You lost the will to fight?

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:13.180
Without... that leek...

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:19.840
Hold on.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:22.550
What?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.010
Kamonegi!
You can still use that leek!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:33.290
Remember our training
with Mr. Gampi!

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:34.760
The Gilgard!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:40.860
Satoshi...

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:44.450
I see... Gilgard, huh?

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.670
Earlade, let’s see
what they can pull off.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.200
Come on! The sword and shield!

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.580
Gilgard! King’s Shield!

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.380
Gilgard! Sacred Sword!

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:29.030
All right! That’s it!
Aim to be Leek Master!

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.070
Can he... battle like that?

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.960
That mockery of a knight
could never beat my Earlade.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.170
Psycho Cutter!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.040
Block it, Kamonegi!

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:47.680
Now! Crossroad Kill!

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.100
We’ll use Crossroad Kill, too!

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.940
So you’re <i>still</i> just
relying on brute-force.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.900
Wow! He’s wielding the
sliced leek like a pro!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.570
Looking good, Kamonegi!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.620
Now he can’t move.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.620
But Earlade can’t, either!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.280
On the contrary.

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:23.670
Earlade’s in the
perfect position to attack.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.380
That’s right! Earlade can...

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.380
Psycho Cutter.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.310
Satoshi!

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.910
He’s just toying with him!

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:40.420
Earlade’s barely even taken any damage!

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:44.690
I wonder what Mr. Gampi would say
if he could see you now.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.510
Are you okay, Kamonegi?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:04.700
You got my hopes up about your potential...
But I must say, I’m a bit disappointed.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:09.090
You’re still far too inadequate a foe
for my Earlade.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.530
Will you continue the battle?

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.600
Stare...

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.690
Yeah! We’re gonna keep going!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.360
Oh, is that a change of attitude I see?

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:33.090
I know how hard
Kamonegi has trained!

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:35.970
I know more than anyone
that he can do better!

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:39.190
Let’s get stronger and stronger,
together!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:46.710
Me and Kamonegi, we’re both inadequate,
but that’s why we’re gonna get stronger!

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.420
I believe in Kamonegi!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.470
You good to go, Kamonegi?

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.060
Verified that Kamonegi
wishes to continue battling.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.610
Here we go,
Rinto! Earlade!

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.830
Then you leave me no choice...

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.820
Earlade. Crossroad Kill!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.790
Detect!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.660
Consecutive Cut!

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:31.510
Infight!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:41.860
All right!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.640
That connected!

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:53.820
Yes... Finish him with Infight!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.090
What?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:03.850
Th-That’s...

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.760
He evolved!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.680
What’s that...?

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.980
Negigaknight! Spot-Billed Duck Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.130
The evolved form of
Galarian Kamonegi!

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:35.950
Only Kamonegi that have survived many battles
can attain this evolution!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.450
Negigaknight!

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:44.990
He responded to your feelings
by evolving.

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.080
What a knight!

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:50.840
Surpassing himself
to protect his lord...

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.170
He has my respect.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.090
Earlade! Crossroad Kill!

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.260
We’ll use Crossroad Kill, too!

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:11.730
You’re still feeling
the damage from before?

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.820
Then, Earlade!
Let down your guard!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.520
He took the hit... on purpose?

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:32.880
Good! This is Earlade’s Ability.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:38.010
I get it.
So that’s why he lowered his guard.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.090
The Ability Heart of Justice.

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:45.790
Being hit by a Evil-type move,
such as Crossroad Kill,

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:49.350
set off his strong sense of justice,
and raised his attack power!

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:52.860
Here it comes!

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.770
Negigaknight!

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.860
Let’s get stronger and stronger!

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.720
Mr. Dande is waiting for us!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:18.380
Crossroad Kill!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:39.430
Earlade is unable to battle!
Negigaknight wins!

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:42.280
As such, the winner is
Contestant Satoshi!

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.370
Whoa, I won!

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.290
You did it, Satoshi!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.480
Based on the results of this battle,

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:59.190
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:10.100
184th!

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:14.690
You have shown me your answer.

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:18.680
We clashed with everything we had...
but we couldn’t win.

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.720
Perhaps we, too,
are still inadequate.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:24.030
Thank you very much.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.950
Here’s hoping we’ll both
keep getting better!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:29.800
Yes!

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:40.680
His evolution into Negigaknight
was so inspiring!

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:42.490
I know, right?

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:49.150
And the way you quipped back at Rinto,
telling him you believe in Kamonegi!

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:51.770
Your words protected Kamonegi!

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.770
And in response, Kamonegi evolved!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:57.270
To protect you, Satoshi!

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:00.070
That true strength of a knight
that Mr. Gampi mentioned...

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:03.700
You really showed it off in that battle!

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.160
R-Right...

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.900
Are you okay,
Negigaknight?

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.820
You see?!

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:24.080
He saved you from yet another pinch!

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.410
Now <i>that’s</i> chivalry!

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.440
Really?

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:34.900
The ardent bond between Satoshi and Kamonegi
led him to evolve into Negigaknight.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:38.360
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:42.620
Look forward to Satoshi’s next battle,
as the fierce clashes continue!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:51.540
Pikachu!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.410
Utsubot!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.120
Transel!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:53.920
Lugia!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:54.710
Achamo!

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:55.500
Morpeko!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.210
Koduck!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.090
Cleffy!

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:57.790
Eevee!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.540
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.210
Teppouo!

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.130
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:00.840
Metagross!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:01.880
Subame!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:02.550
Me...

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:03.800
Metamon!

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:20.570
Pikachu!

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:21.400
Usohachi!

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:22.110
Chicorita!

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:22.900
Tamatama!

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:23.650
Mamepato!

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:24.490
Togedemaru!

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:25.240
Lucario!

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.030
Odoshishi!

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:26.820
Seadra!

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:27.450
Laplace!

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.280
Starmie!

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.080
Miniryu!

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:29.870
Windie!

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:30.580
Iwark!

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:31.410
Kucheat!

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:32.160
Togekiss!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:32.910
Sleep!

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.660
Ptera!

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:34.500
Raikou!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.250
U'u!

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.040
Wooloo!

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:36.830
Ruriri!

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:37.580
Leafia!

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:38.380
Armorgaw!

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.170
Abagoura!

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:39.960
Latias!

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:40.710
Spear!

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:41.460
Agnome!

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:42.210
Muma!

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:43.300
Madatsubomi!

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:44.460
Mew!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.600
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:15.520
Be it plumbing or Pokémon-sitting,
you can leave it all to us!

00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:17.790
We’re the Plusle and Minun
handymen!

00:23:17.790 --> 00:23:19.250
It’s a Plusle and Minun!

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:20.650
They’re really cute.

00:23:20.650 --> 00:23:21.840
Wha—?!

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.120
Nyarth!

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:24.110
Come on...

00:23:24.110 --> 00:23:25.090
Go, let’s help him.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:29.230
Plusle... Minun...
I’m going to do my best!

00:23:29.230 --> 00:23:30.930
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:34.480
Leave It All to Us!
The Plusle and Minun Handymen!!
